{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/javaScript-closures/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Personal Blog"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"73f92d99-43a7-5f5e-b757-3e258e049e90","excerpt":"In this blog, i'll try to document what closures are, how they work, and why they're useful, using simple language and examples. What Is a Closure? A closure is…","html":"<p>In this blog, i'll try to document what closures are, how they work, and why they're useful, using simple language and examples.</p>\n<h2>What Is a Closure?</h2>\n<p>A <strong>closure</strong> is a function that remembers the variables from the place where it was created, even if it's used somewhere else. This means the function keeps access to the variables from its original scope.</p>\n<p>In simple terms, a closure allows you to:</p>\n<ul style=\"margin-left: 30px;\">\n  <li>Access outer function's variables from an inner function.</li>\n  <li>Preserve data in a function even after the outer function has finished running.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How Do Closures Work?</h2>\n<p>In JavaScript, when you create a function inside another function, the inner function has access to:</p>\n<ul style=\"margin-left: 30px;\">\n <li> Its own variables.</li>\n <li> Variables in the outer function.</li>\n <li> Global variables.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Even after the outer function has completed, the inner function can still access the outer function's variables. This happens because the variables are stored in a closure.</p>\n<h2>Why Use Closures?</h2>\n<p>Closures are useful because they let you:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Create private variables</strong>: Variables that can't be accessed from outside a function.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintain state between function calls</strong>: Remember data without using global variables.</li>\n<li><strong>Avoid polluting the global scope</strong>: Keep your code clean and organized.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Examples of Closures</h2>\n<p>Let's look at some simple examples to understand closures better.</p>\n<h3>Example 1: Private Variables</h3>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">createCounter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">let</span> count <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token number\">0</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// This is a private variable</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">function</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    count<span class=\"token operator\">++</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>count<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> counter <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">createCounter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token function\">counter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 1</span>\n<span class=\"token function\">counter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 2</span>\n<span class=\"token function\">counter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 3</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>We have a function <code class=\"language-text\">createCounter</code> that defines a variable <code class=\"language-text\">count</code>.\n<code class=\"language-text\">createCounter</code> returns an inner function that increases <code class=\"language-text\">count</code> and logs it.\nEven after <code class=\"language-text\">createCounter</code> has finished running, the inner function still remembers <code class=\"language-text\">count</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Example 2: Creating Functions with Preset Values</h2>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">makeMultiplier</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">x</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">function</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">y</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> x <span class=\"token operator\">*</span> y<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> double <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">makeMultiplier</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">2</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> triple <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">makeMultiplier</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">3</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\nconsole<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token function\">double</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">5</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 10</span>\nconsole<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token function\">triple</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">5</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 15</span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">makeMultiplier</code> is a function that takes a number <code class=\"language-text\">x</code> and returns a new function.\nThe returned function takes another number <code class=\"language-text\">y</code> and returns <code class=\"language-text\">x</code> multiplied by <code class=\"language-text\">y</code>.\nThe functions <code class=\"language-text\">double</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">triple</code> remember the value of <code class=\"language-text\">x</code> they were created with.</p>\n<h2>Applications</h2>\n<h3>Memoization</h3>\n<p>Memoization is an optimization technique that caches the results of expensive function calls and returns the cached result when the same inputs occur again. Closures help in maintaining the cache state.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">memoize</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">fn</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> cache <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">function</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\"><span class=\"token operator\">...</span>args</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> key <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token constant\">JSON</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">stringify</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>args<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>cache<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>key<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> cache<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>key<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> result <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">fn</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">apply</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> args<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    cache<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>key<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> result<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> result<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">fibonacci</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">n</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>n <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;=</span> <span class=\"token number\">1</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> n<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token function\">fibonacci</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>n <span class=\"token operator\">-</span> <span class=\"token number\">1</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">+</span> <span class=\"token function\">fibonacci</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>n <span class=\"token operator\">-</span> <span class=\"token number\">2</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> memoizedFibonacci <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">memoize</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>fibonacci<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\nconsole<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token function\">memoizedFibonacci</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">40</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 102334155</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The memoize function returns a new function that wraps the original fn.\nIt uses a closure to store a cache object that holds previously computed results.</p>\n<h3>Module Pattern</h3>\n<p>The Module Pattern uses closures to encapsulate private variables and expose public methods, promoting better code organization and preventing global namespace pollution.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> CounterModule <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">function</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">let</span> count <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token number\">0</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Private variable</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">increment</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    count<span class=\"token operator\">++</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>count<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">reset</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    count <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token number\">0</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'Counter reset'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    increment<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    reset\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\nCounterModule<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">increment</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 1</span>\nCounterModule<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">increment</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: 2</span>\nCounterModule<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">reset</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>     <span class=\"token comment\">// Output: Counter reset</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expression) creates a private scope.\ncount, increment, and reset are encapsulated within this scope.\nOnly increment and reset are exposed, while count remains private</p>\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>Closures are an important concept in JavaScript that allow functions to remember the environment where they were created. They help you write more flexible and powerful code by giving you access to outer variables even after those functions have finished running.\nMore on closures can be found <a href=\"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/lets-learn-javascript-closures-66feb44f6a44/\">here</a></p>","frontmatter":{"title":"JavaScript Closures","date":"November 13, 2023","description":null}},"previous":null,"next":{"fields":{"slug":"/big-data-hackathon/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"My first Big Data hackathon!"}}},"pageContext":{"id":"73f92d99-43a7-5f5e-b757-3e258e049e90","previousPostId":null,"nextPostId":"70fd7550-4da2-563c-8d6f-f43ba19df8e9"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2841359383","3257411868"],"slicesMap":{}}